{
  "name": "Islanded 8-60-10 MW ramp - sequential commitment and release",
  "description": "Islanded 5 × 15 MW gas-turbine fleet, 15 MW solar, 18 MW / 8 MWh grid-forming BESS. Two jobs — job-base (800 nodes, t = 0) and job-01 (200 nodes, t = 35 s) — carry no end event and establish a permanent 1,000-node floor (10.5 MW compute, PUE-inclusive) that runs throughout the full 90-min run without shedding. Additional 200-node GPU jobs arrive every ~35 s from t = 35 s, driving a staircase ramp from 10.5 MW to 63.0 MW (6,000 nodes) by t = 15 min. A 5-min peak hold follows, then a symmetric staircase shed (one job every ~40 s) returns cluster compute to the 10.5 MW floor by t = 39 min. The final 51-min hold is deliberate: t_min_run_s (1,800 s) must elapse on the last-committed turbine for the decommitment sequence to complete inside the run window.",
